     I can't recall ever hearing about it.  The paper
appears to have been formatted with something which
produces fi and ff ligatures, probably TeX, then scanned
from hardcopy with software which couldn't recognize such
things.  So there are consistent misspellings in various
words, like "quantication" everywhere that "quantification"
is intended; the "fi" is always missing. For a while I was
wondering whether language parsing had coined a bunch of
strange new words....



